  "chapter": {
    "bookTitle": "1 Chronicles",
    "delineation": "Chapter",
    "number": 18,
    "summary": "David subdues all the adversaries of Israel and reigns in justice over the people.",
    "chapterAugmentations": [],
    "verses": [
      {
        "text": "Now after this it came to pass, that David smote the Philistines, and subdued them, and took Gath and her towns out of the hand of the Philistines.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 43,
            "end": 48,
            "text": "2 Sam. 8:1 (1–18)."
          },
          {
            "start": 93,
            "end": 97,
            "text": "1 Sam. 17:4."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 1,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "1 Sam. 17:4.",
            "prettyString": "1 Samuel 17:4",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "1samuel",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 17,
                    "end": 17,
                    "verses": [
                      {
                        "start": 4,
                        "end": 4
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "1 Chronicles 18:1",
        "book": "1 Chronicles",
        "chapter": 18,
        "verse": 1
      },
      {
        "text": "And he smote Moab; and the Moabites became David’s servants, and brought gifts.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 61,
            "end": 64
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 2,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "1 Chronicles 18:2",
        "book": "1 Chronicles",
        "chapter": 18,
        "verse": 2
      },
      {
        "text": "And David smote Hadarezer king of Zobah unto Hamath, as he went to stablish his dominion by the river Euphrates.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 3,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "1 Chronicles 18:3",
        "book": "1 Chronicles",
        "chapter": 18,
        "verse": 3
      },
      {
        "text": "And David took from him a thousand chariots, and seven thousand horsemen, and twenty thousand footmen: David also houghed all the chariot horses, but reserved of them an hundred chariots.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 138,
            "end": 145
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 4,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "1 Chronicles 18:4",
        "book": "1 Chronicles",
        "chapter": 18,
        "verse": 4
      },
      {
        "text": "And when the Syrians of Damascus came to help Hadarezer king of Zobah, David slew of the Syrians two and twenty thousand men.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 5,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "1 Chronicles 18:5",
        "book": "1 Chronicles",
        "chapter": 18,
        "verse": 5
      },
      {
        "text": "Then David put garrisons in Syria-damascus; and the Syrians became David’s servants, and brought gifts. Thus the Lord preserved David whithersoever he went.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 15,
            "end": 24
          },
          {
            "start": 85,
            "end": 88
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 6,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "1 Chronicles 18:6",
        "book": "1 Chronicles",
        "chapter": 18,
        "verse": 6
      },
      {
        "text": "And David took the shields of gold that were on the servants of Hadarezer, and brought them to Jerusalem.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 7,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "1 Chronicles 18:7",
        "book": "1 Chronicles",
        "chapter": 18,
        "verse": 7
      },
      {
        "text": "Likewise from Tibhath, and from Chun, cities of Hadarezer, brought David very much brass, wherewith Solomon made the brasen sea, and the pillars, and the vessels of brass.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 100,
            "end": 107,
            "text": "2 Ne. 5:16."
          },
          {
            "start": 124,
            "end": 127,
            "text": "1 Kgs. 7:23; 2 Chr. 4:15 (12–16)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 8,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "2 Ne. 5:16.",
            "prettyString": "2 Nephi 5:16",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "2nephi",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 5,
                    "end": 5,
                    "verses": [
                      {
                        "start": 16,
                        "end": 16
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "1 Chronicles 18:8",
        "book": "1 Chronicles",
        "chapter": 18,
        "verse": 8
      },
      {
        "text": "Now when Tou king of Hamath heard how David had smitten all the host of Hadarezer king of Zobah;",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 9,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "1 Chronicles 18:9",
        "book": "1 Chronicles",
        "chapter": 18,
        "verse": 9
      },
      {
        "text": "He sent Hadoram his son to king David, to inquire of his welfare, and to congratulate him, because he had fought against Hadarezer, and smitten him; (for Hadarezer had war with Tou;) and with him all manner of vessels of gold and silver and brass.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 187,
            "end": 195
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 10,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "1 Chronicles 18:10",
        "book": "1 Chronicles",
        "chapter": 18,
        "verse": 10
      },
      {
        "text": "Them also king David dedicated unto the Lord, with the silver and the gold that he brought from all these nations; from Edom, and from Moab, and from the children of Ammon, and from the Philistines, and from Amalek.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 100,
            "end": 105
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 11,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "1 Chronicles 18:11",
        "book": "1 Chronicles",
        "chapter": 18,
        "verse": 11
      },
      {
        "text": "Moreover Abishai the son of Zeruiah slew of the Edomites in the valley of salt eighteen thousand.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 12,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "1 Chronicles 18:12",
        "book": "1 Chronicles",
        "chapter": 18,
        "verse": 12
      },
      {
        "text": "And he put garrisons in Edom; and all the Edomites became David’s servants. Thus the Lord preserved David whithersoever he went.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 42,
            "end": 50,
            "text": "1 Kgs. 11:15."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 13,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "1 Kgs. 11:15.",
            "prettyString": "1 Kings 11:15",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "1kings",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 11,
                    "end": 11,
                    "verses": [
                      {
                        "start": 15,
                        "end": 15
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "1 Chronicles 18:13",
        "book": "1 Chronicles",
        "chapter": 18,
        "verse": 13
      },
      {
        "text": "So David reigned over all Israel, and executed judgment and justice among all his people.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 14,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "1 Chronicles 18:14",
        "book": "1 Chronicles",
        "chapter": 18,
        "verse": 14
      },
      {
        "text": "And Joab the son of Zeruiah was over the host; and Jehoshaphat the son of Ahilud, recorder.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 28,
            "end": 31
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 15,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "1 Chronicles 18:15",
        "book": "1 Chronicles",
        "chapter": 18,
        "verse": 15
      },
      {
        "text": "And Zadok the son of Ahitub, and Abimelech the son of Abiathar, were the priests; and Shavsha was scribe;",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 64,
            "end": 68
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 16,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "1 Chronicles 18:16",
        "book": "1 Chronicles",
        "chapter": 18,
        "verse": 16
      },
      {
        "text": "And Benaiah the son of Jehoiada was over the Cherethites and the Pelethites; and the sons of David were chief about the king.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 32,
            "end": 35
          },
          {
            "start": 99,
            "end": 103
          }
        ],
